[statement]
Of two versions of one package providing a name alike, the one installed
is kept, whatever their priorities: `c` 1, installed, and `c` 3 provide
`w` at no version, `c` 3 with the higher priority, and the world's `w`
keeps `c` 1. Of two packages of different names at no version, the higher
priority goes first, installed or not
(`a-higher-priority-outranks-an-installed-provider-at-no-version`).

[repository]
P:c
V:3
k:10
p:w

P:b
V:1

[installed]
P:c
V:1
k:5
p:w

[world]
w

